<script setup>import e from '../data/report-evidence.json';const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL</script>
<template><div class="stack"><div class="row spread"><p class="formula">(E₁,z₁), (E₂,z₂), … → (E₁,z₂), (E₂,z₃), …</p><a :href="base+'evidence/phase2_diag.txt'" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="small">Open literal diagnostic</a></div><div class="split grow"><table class="evidence-table"><thead><tr><th>Flow-mode condition</th><th class="numeric">PSNR ↑</th><th class="numeric">NLL ↓</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr v-for="r in e.pairingDiagnostic" :key="r.name"><td>{{r.name}}</td><td class="numeric">{{r.psnr.toFixed(3)}}</td><td class="numeric">{{r.nll.toFixed(3)}}</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="col"><h2>Pairing changes have little effect in this diagnostic.</h2><p>Shifting historical z vectors changes PSNR from 23.562 to 23.543 dB. NLL changes from 2.642 to 2.640.</p><p class="note">This suggests weak use of the relationship between each historical image and its edit. It does not prove that history has no effect: replacing the user’s history lowers performance.</p></div></div><div class="rule"><h3>Decoder noise sensitivity</h3><div class="chips"><span v-for="r in e.robustness.rows" :key="r.scale">{{r.scale}} × std → {{r.psnr.toFixed(3)}} dB</span></div></div><p class="small muted">Archived diagnostic: 120 queries, 24 per expert; noise test: 10 images. These values remain separate from the report’s rounded ablation table.</p></div></template>
